📊 Complaint Q&A Assistant - RAG Model (Retriever + Generator)
This project utilizes a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline to answer customer complaints related to financial products. By integrating FAISS (or ChromaDB) for efficient vector search, and FLAN-T5 for text generation, the system answers questions from real complaint data.

The Gradio interface provides a user-friendly platform for live Q&A.

chnologies Used
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): Data cleaning, processing, and feature extraction to prepare customer complaints for use in a machine learning model.s

FAISS (or ChromaDB) for efficient nearest neighbor search and retrieval of similar complaint chunks.

Sentence-Transformers for embedding textual data (turning customer complaints into vector representations).

FLAN-T5 (via Hugging Face’s Transformers) for natural language text generation.

Gradio for the interactive user interface.

📌 Steps Involved in the Project

1. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
   Objective: Understand and clean the data.
   Data Collection: Collect customer complaints, including Narrative Text, Product, Sub-product, and Issue details.

Data Cleaning:

Handle missing values, duplicate rows, and irrelevant data.

Preprocess narrative text: lowercasing, removing special characters, and boilerplate text (e.g., "Dear Sir/Madam").

Feature Extraction:

Split complaints into meaningful chunks.

Identify and clean categorical variables like product names.

Tools:
Pandas, Numpy for data manipulation

Regex for text cleaning
Building the FAISS Index
Objective: Create a vector store to retrieve similar complaint chunks.
Text Embedding: Use Sentence-Transformers to convert complaint narratives into vector representations.

Index Creation: Build a FAISS index to enable fast similarity search.

Storage: Save the FAISS index for later use.

3. Building the RAG Pipeline
   Objective: Integrate a Retriever and Generator for live Q&A.
   Retriever: Use FAISS (or ChromaDB) to retrieve the top k complaint chunks based on the user's query.

Generator: Use FLAN-T5 to generate answers from the retrieved complaint chunks.

Prompting: Build a clear prompt that combines the retrieved chunks and the user’s question.

Gradio UI for Live Q&A
Objective: Build a Gradio interface for interactive Q&A.
User Input: Allows users to type their questions.

Answer Generation: Uses the RAG pipeline to generate answers based on retrieved complaint chunks.

Display: Shows both the answer and the relevant context.
